 "technique": {
  "title": "Shift in the gap",
  "feel": "After each long note, lift and move the whole arm to the next position: thumb to G, then thumb to F, then back to C. Look ahead at the staff during the long note."
 },
 "theory": [
  {
   "q": "Position shift",
   "a": "Real music rarely stays under five fingers. Players move the hand during long notes or rests. The fingering numbers tell you where a new position starts: a sudden finger 1 on a higher note means \"move here\"."
  }
 ],
 "intro": "One piece, three hand positions: C, then G, then F with its B flat, then home. The first real test of reading while moving.",
